  "body": "Stacks on nothing; the row hunk sits after the row's `ui.horizontal` block in `chips`, clear of infield's #1701 hunks (their changes are inside the block). Does not touch #1710's files.\n\nWhat changed: when the viewport pointer is over a picked face, chain or vertex (`State.hover`, same entity and feature), that pick's Geometry-tab row gets an outline in the selection ink and is recorded in the new ephemeral `State.geo_row_marked` (cleared at the frame edge in `shell.rs`). Leaving the viewport clears it. No command, no snapshot PNG.\n\nPinned by: `geo_row_hover::viewport_hover_over_a_picked_face_marks_its_row` (hovers the real viewport over the top face in Faces mode: only the face row is marked, no command filed, cleared on leaving). Mutation-checked: deleting the push, dropping the feature match, and deleting the per-frame clear each turn it red.\n\nNot exercised: chain and vertex rows in the viewport (same code path, one test), full application GPU screenshots. Quick gate passed against `upstream/main` for the author-side review fix.\n\nChangelog: Hovering a picked face, edge or corner in the viewport marks its row in the Geometry tab.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1519\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n## Review screenshots\n\nThese captures show the real Geometry panel from the existing viewport-hover test. The test uses real face picking. Its viewport is a placeholder, so the images are cropped to the panel and do not show the GPU model render. Before captures temporarily suppress only the new outline. After captures use the PR behavior. Capture instrumentation is not committed.\n\n| Pointer state | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| At rest | ![Before: At rest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/before/rest.png) | ![After: At rest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/after/rest.png) |\n| Over the selected face | ![Before: Over the selected face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/before/hover.png) | ![After: Over the selected face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/after/hover.png) |\n| After leaving the viewport | ![Before: After leaving the viewport](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/before/left.png) | ![After: After leaving the viewport](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d7f7b237ee8c632234fae67a0945cf057ee76c78/docs/pr-1711/after/left.png) |\n\nThe review fix also restores main's CRLF line endings in `shell.rs`. The intended row-state clear remains. The semantic merge conflict is deferred to the merge turn as requested; this author-side pass does not merge.\n",
